                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course aims to cultivate a patient-centered approach to core communication competencies. It systematically covers doctor-patient relationships, communication principles, and practical techniques for key clinical scenarios such as patient interviewing, information delivery, and shared decision-making. Through diverse methods like case studies, role-playing, and simulation training, students can safely translate theory into practice. The course is designed to enhance empathy, collaboration, and humanistic professionalism among medical students and healthcare practitioners, laying a solid foundation for becoming outstanding medical professionals who excel in both technical expertise and communication.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
